From b8f794a65a7b0cf964298ebabb207b011978dddc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Varun-iiitb <var3907@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:53:42 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 21/68] LivenessMetricsStore: persisted anonymised liveness
 metrics

The engine's LivenessMetrics live in memory for one process. The store
keeps their totals in SharedPreferences (liveness_metrics) across app
restarts: counts and totals only (sessions, passes by path, final and
attempt failures by error code, retries, cancellations, device errors,
analysed frames and processing time, challenge counts and time). No
session ids, timestamps, scores of individuals or images.

merge(metrics) adds what a LivenessMetrics object gained since its
previous merge (weakly keyed per object), so each count is added once,
whatever the number of services. derived() returns the totals and the
rates: avg processing ms, avg challenge completion ms, retry rate,
failure rate, passive share, failures by code. reset() clears the totals;
counts already merged are not added again.

Tests (JVM, in-memory SharedPreferences): each count once, merge across
two services, persistence across a new store and a new service, reset,
and only count keys with long values stored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
